WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.982
"The Safety and Efficacy of Ketogenic,
Low-Carb Diets for Diabetes Remission"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.680
The effect of a plant-based,
low-fat diet

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.920
versus an animal-based,
ketogenic diet

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.200
on caloric intake
and weight loss.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.000
A plant-based diet without
sugary refined grain foods

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.280
versus a keto diet
with a lot of vegetables.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.480
After two weeks randomized
to one of the two diets,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.960
the participants were switched
to the other one

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.640
for another two weeks.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.920
Looking at the scale, guess
who lost more body weight?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.160
Those on the low-carb diet.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.480
But guess who lost
more body fat?

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.880
Those on the low-fat diet.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.040
In fact, there was
no significant fat loss

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.640
on the low-carb diet,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.480
whereas two pounds
(1 kg) of fat were lost

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.240
on the low-fat diet.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.320
What they were losing
on the low-carb diet

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.320
was fat-free mass,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.920
like water weight
but muscle, too.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.560
While fat-free mass
was relatively preserved

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.480
while on the low-fat diet,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.600
fat-free mass decreased
on the low-carb diet,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.200
and there was evidence
that the participants

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.440
were losing muscle mass
despite eating more protein

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.680
than when they were
on the plant-based diet.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.000
But when they were eating
almost no carbs,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.800
their blood sugars
were certainly lower.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.400
Does a ketogenic diet
have a place

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.560
within diabetes
clinical practice?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.560
It's even been suggested
that low-carb diets

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.880
could put type 2 diabetes
into remission,

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.680
which can be defined
as an HbA1c,

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.600
a marker
of blood sugar control,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.480
lower than 6.5 percent
for at least three months

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.400
after stopping any blood
sugar-lowering medications.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.880
But high blood sugars
are just the symptom.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.240
The disease is one
of carbohydrate intolerance.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.600
If you're allergic to peanuts

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.440
and don't have symptoms
because you avoid peanuts,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.040
you're just
managing the disease,

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.560
not curing it.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.160
Curing a peanut allergy

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.640
would mean being able
to eat peanuts like anyone

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.040
without a peanut allergy.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.320
It's the same with carbohydrates
and type 2 diabetes.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.240
True remission
would be being able

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.800
to eat carbohydrates
like everyone else

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.440
without getting adverse effects.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.080
As Dr. Greger has covered,

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.960
low-carb diets can actually
make diabetes worse,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.320
worsening insulin resistance

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.760
and increasing intolerance
to carbohydrates.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.040
That would only
be a problem, though,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.360
if you resumed
eating carbohydrates.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.800
Why not just stick
to a ketogenic diet forever?

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.040
What is the efficacy
and safety of low-carb diets

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.760
for type 2 diabetes remission?

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.160
First of all, it didn't work.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.160
Using the,
"Under 6 .5 percent

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.240
and off all
diabetes medications"

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.800
definition of remission,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.200
there was no significant
effect at six months

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.160
and at 12 months
there was less remission,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.280
meaning more diabetes
in the low-carb groups,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.480
along with clinically important
harms on quality of life

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.200
and, the deal-killer,
an increase in LDL cholesterol.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.400
LDL cholesterol,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.480
commonly known
as bad cholesterol,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.360
is unequivocally recognized
as the principal driving force

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.520
in the development
of atherosclerotic

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.960
cardiovascular disease,

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.120
the leading cause of death
for both men and women.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.280
Basically, we should try
to get our LDL

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.040
as low as possible.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.200
Lower for longer is better.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.280
Even if our LDL is normal,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.960
even if other
heart disease risk factors

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.480
are considered optimal,

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.000
it is of utmost importance
to control our LDL.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.840
If LDL is the primary driver
of our primary killer,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.240
then if we could just know
one thing about a diet,

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.480
if there were only
one question we could ask

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.600
about some new diet
someone tells us about,

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.680
it would be,
"What does this diet do

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.160
to my LDL cholesterol?"

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.960
If you follow people
on lower carb diets over time

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.920
and see what happens

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.320
to their coronary artery
calcium scores,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.760
which signify the progression
of coronary artery disease,

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.200
you'll find
that the low-carb group

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.320
had the highest incidence

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.280
of coronary artery
calcium worsening,

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.480
though this was only the case

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.320
with animal-based
low-carb diets,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.120
not plant-based ones.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.040
But those who started
eating low-carb diets

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.480
rich in animal protein and fat

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.960
in early adulthood,
had an increased risk

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.960
of coronary artery
calcium progression

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.960
in middle age.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.400
Of course, all carbs
are not created equal.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.240
Carbs that are
detrimental to our health,

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.400
like sugars and refined grains,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.280
need to be distinguished

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.600
from those
with beneficial effects.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.520
When the American
Heart Association

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.160
looked at dietary patterns
at a population level

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.480
and ranked them from
the most to the least aligned

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:31.440
with its dietary guidance
for heart health,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.240
how did
low-carbohydrate diets rank?

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.600
Poorly.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.880
In fact,
they were ranked the worst.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.480
Even when very low-carb diets
are followed optimally,

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.400
they promote restriction
of foods considered

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.680
essential to heart health,

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.320
like legumes and whole grains,

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.320
and include
high-saturated-fat sources

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.600
like meat and dairy,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.867
which are both
strongly discouraged.

